{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/89194-exploit-solitary-confinement-neeeeed-help","id":89194,"title":"Exploit: Solitary Confinement - Neeeeed Help!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-11T20:03:51-07:00","id":89194,"title":"Exploit: Solitary Confinement - Neeeeed Help!","content":"A vampire in my group who has a ghoul NPC played by the Story Teller/ (Co-story teller depending on who's turn it is ) This Ghoul was sucked into confinement for 10 days and Ended the chapter, giving experience. The game is over and we had the player roll for her ghoul and he has made the meditation check to not go cuckoo bananas, but the story teller said that he would die after 3 days without water. The player then asked if she could take the True Friend Merit so that the ST couldnt kill the ghoul. ( to which the GM replied no ) Would there be other ways to keep this ghoul alive? Would he actually starve to death in this supernatural rift? Options?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;&quot;The demon gestures at a target and opens a rift in reality \u2014 a black pit of nothing where the person<br /> remains trapped. The oubliette doesn\u2019t keep a victim incarcerated indefinitely, but it creates a place of<br /> perfect sensory deprivation. The victim cannot hear, see or feel anything, even sound or sensation that<br /> he creates. Even if the target only remains in the oubliette for a matter of minutes, the experience saps<br /> his will and can drive him mad.<br /> <br /> Success: The target falls into the oubliette. An observer sees the demon point or glare at the target, and<br /> then the target vanish as though pulled backward by a powerful force. While in the void, the target<br /> experiences no sensory input \u2014 even if the target bites his own hand, he feels nothing. Even if he<br /> screams, everything around him is silent. This is, of course, extremely disconcerting; the target<br /> experiences a breaking point (p. XX) every hour he remains confined. The Storyteller should apply a<br /> negative modifier to the roll of at least one die, possibly more if the character has a special reason to<br /> fear the dark, sensory deprivation, kidnapping, etc. The target remains trapped for a number of hours<br /> equal to the demon\u2019s Primum, though the demon can cancel the effect earlier if she wishes &quot;&quot; <br /> <br /> True Friend (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Effect: Your character has a true friend. While that friend may<br /> have specific functions covered by other Merits (Allies, Contacts,<br /> Retainer, Mentor, et cetera), True Friend represents a deeper,<br /> truly trusting relationship that cannot be breached. Unless your<br /> character does something egregious to cause it, her True Friend will<br /> not betray her. The Storyteller cannot kill a True Friend as part of a<br /> plot without your express permission. Any rolls to influence a True<br /> Friend against your character suffer a \u20135 die penalty. In addition,<br /> once per story your character can regain one spent Willpower by<br /> having a meaningful interaction with her True Friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T20:47:13-07:00","id":89214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/89194-exploit-solitary-confinement-neeeeed-help#post89194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game is over and we had the player roll for her ghoul and he has made the meditation check to not go cuckoo bananas, but the story teller said that he would die after 3 days without water</div> </div> </div> </div>The Storyteller's full of shit, bluntly put:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>World of Darkness Core Rulebook, pg175, &quot;Deprivation&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character can go a number of days equal to his Stamina before being inhibited by lack of water. Once that threshold is exceeded, he suffers one point of bashing damage for each day that passes. He can go without food for a number of days equal to his Stamina + Resolve. After that point, he suffers another point of bashing damage a day. Denied both food and water, he suffers two bashing wounds a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the ghoul was already severely deprived <i>and</i> severely damaged, three days without water would not kill them, even before getting into whether Solitary Confinement applies any physical effects in light of how Unchained magic usually works with regard to time and biology and the like - Boltholes being the operative comparison.<br /> <br /> Considering that being trapped for ten <i>days</i> requires a) an exceptional success and b) a Primum of 10, I have to ask what the devil is going on in this game and whether the ST doesn't just want the NPC to die but is inexplicably neglecting the power of ST fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-11-2014, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T20:56:56-07:00","id":89226,"title":"","content":"I don't quite understand how the ghoul was affected for 10 *days* by an Exploit whose effect is listed in the rules as lasting for a number of *hours* equal to the demon's Primum, but I suppose that it could have been Storyteller's fiat in the interest of telling a particular tale. There doesn't appear to be anything in the rules that would indicate that a person trapped within would be subject to hunger or thirst (which could be an oversight due to it very rarely being relevant with a power that lasts for mere hours rather than days), but I would personally feel that the need for food, water, etc would be held at bay by supernatural means. After all, there's no mention in the text of being without air, implying that there is at least SOME level of life-support in the rift.<br /> <br /> That said, it sounds to me like your Storyteller just wants to get rid of this particular ghoul for some reason.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2495-rumanchu","name":"rumanchu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T21:20:28-07:00","id":89235,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you havean asshole Storyteller, my friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T03:39:15-07:00","id":89377,"title":"","content":"A-hole Storyteller here to give my side...<br /> <br /> a) The demon was so powerful, as some have noticed, because the group is all sitting at 30-35+ XP each, some even more than that. I had them go up against a Primum 6 demon with a number of cultists, and the demon was dead within the first move of combat. Just trying to give them a good challenge. I may have overdone it, I admit, but that is simply a flaw in my attempts to learn the balance of combat, and not anything malicious. <br /> <br /> b) The reason the ghoul was trapped for 10 days was because the demon got an incredibly lucky roll and the ghoul got an incredibly unlucky one. It was a fluke, but he was pulled into solitary confinement to help with the battle, as he is really powerful and the demon was aware of this and wanted to remove him as a threat. My intention was not to trap him for a week and a half, just remove him from that combat. But hey, stuff happens, and sometimes a really unlucky roll can be the end for someone.<br /> <br /> c) He is NOT a NPC. He has been a consistent, played character for 3 campaigns, with the same consideration and XP rewards that the rest of the group gets. He goes well beyond the confines of the Retainer merit he was purchased with. He's a PC. That seems pretty obvious to me.<br /> <br /> d) True Friend says the ST can't kill that character as part of the &quot;plot.&quot; A character dying due to involving himself in combat is not plot in the sense I believe they are thinking of. Plot would be me killing him as a device in the story, outside of player control. And even if it were, then giving True Friend to a player character makes them unkillable, which is absurd. As I state to you, Vitalis, then all the players could just take True Friend for each other, and there would no longer be any risk of death. I'm not saying all PCs should be easily killed, but there should be a risk.<br /> <br /> e) I can see the argument that the Solitary Confinement could work like a Bolthole and negate the need for food. I had not considered that and had Vitalis brought it up when we talked about this earlier, I likely would have agreed. It's a valid point.<br /> <br /> f) Vitalis, I already told you he could survive or be saved, so I'm not sure why you felt the need to come on here and prove me wrong. *thumbs up*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2101-reverendk","name":"ReverendK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T03:58:50-07:00","id":89379,"title":"","content":"Still not sure how he can have been trapped for 10 days? The power traps him for 6 hours if it's a Primum 6 demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T05:11:35-07:00","id":89401,"title":"","content":"Okay, one, lets not call people an a-hole ever again. Especially when they're not around. That kind of thing is what gives forums like this a bad name.<br /> <br /> Two, to me, it sounds like saving the ghoul is possible as a side quest thing. If its possible to do, then there should be no real problem. Better to save him than having him flat out dead.<br /> <br /> Three, I think having the players ask to apply the True Friend merit retroactively to a character after something happened, PC or NPC, is a bit odd. I'd have flat out forbidden that too.<br /> <br /> Four, all STs have final say over powers in their game. The timing thing sounds a bit suspect, but its livable. Trying to force an ST to conform to exact wording of a power in a book that's not even in its final form, then calling him names over it, is BS.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's a big difference between someone arranging a story way to have a way to save endangered character, and an ST who sets up a death trap and insta-kills a character for not doing exactly what the ST wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-12-2014, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T06:53:48-07:00","id":89448,"title":"","content":"I think I'm going to second what MCN said.<br /> As for the ghoul, as an ST my own preference would be to just say that he doesn't suffer from those things in there (especially in light of the powerup, making it comparable to a bolthole) or I would make it a session in and off itself, saving him from it.<br /> Perhaps another demon offers to help in exchange for a service? There are options.<br /> Could also have him come out deprived and sick, but alive thanks to vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T08:14:44-07:00","id":89493,"title":"","content":"Please don't use this to attack anyone. Not the point of this at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I did not post the whole story as it would take too much time. Yes the Demon had primum 10 and Yes it was totally an exceptional success so it was legit 10 days. Yes our characters have close to 40 exp as we have been playing them for like EVER..<br /> George (the ghoul) was created with a retainer merit and has been passed around the table as to who plays him. One person dealt with his actions and dice in combat. Another person voiced him here and there when he decided he needed to speak ( which was super rare, because i was busy playing my character, my PC ) I would consider that more of an NPC than a PC, but eitherway. I can see how it could be consider PC.<br /> <br /> These forums are not intended to be full of drama and shenanigans. I know name calling is an easy route, but its not really helpful.<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for those who gave input on the deprivation and thank you to the person who posted the rules on what that means. Thank you for the bolthole Idea too. I had not thought of that either. I was wondering if there had been life support in there. I knew this book was not fully fleshed out so I was wondering about Options and what happens and if there was anything I hadnt thought about.<br /> <br /> and Mr. K I did not come here to &quot;prove you wrong&quot; I came to see if there was a legit way to save him other than DM magic he is saved huzzah!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-12-2014, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}